    {
      "id": "oz5CRbdF7zkac5prfjc4o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -580,
      "y": 2143,
      "width": 435.6396484375,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1rG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1887845920,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 492403232,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794253104236,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "grwbKind": "answer"
      },
      "text": "Beekeeping. Your words went in on the right.\n\nA crowd on the front of a hive on a hot\nday looks alarming. It's called bearding,\nand it's usually just bees cooling off.\nThat's your long queue.\n\nA hive can lose its queen and still look\nbusy. Nurse bees with no brood to tend\nturn to foraging, so traffic carries on.\nThat's #287: looked fine, nothing finishing.\n\nSo keepers don't judge by the bee count.\nThey open the hive and look for fresh eggs.\nEggs hatch in about 3 days, so eggs mean\nthe queen was laying in the last 3 days.\nSealed brood only proves she was there\nup to 3 weeks ago.\n\nThis fits \"nothing finishing\" only.\nIt says nothing about your mute/add loop.\n\nYour turn. For invoices, what is your\n\"fresh eggs\"?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Beekeeping. Your words went in on the right.\n\nA crowd on the front of a hive on a hot\nday looks alarming. It's called bearding,\nand it's usually just bees cooling off.\nThat's your long queue.\n\nA hive can lose its queen and still look\nbusy. Nurse bees with no brood to tend\nturn to foraging, so traffic carries on.\nThat's #287: looked fine, nothing finishing.\n\nSo keepers don't judge by the bee count.\nThey open the hive and look for fresh eggs.\nEggs hatch in about 3 days, so eggs mean\nthe queen was laying in the last 3 days.\nSealed brood only proves she was there\nup to 3 weeks ago.\n\nThis fits \"nothing finishing\" only.\nIt says nothing about your mute/add loop.\n\nYour turn. For invoices, what is your\n\"fresh eggs\"?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fTjNSIeGBPez-9LKx1_IL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -580.18017578125,
      "y": 2781,
      "width": 552.9595947265625,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c1rH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1147483680,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1953711072,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794253130526,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ok bees. did not see that coming. the queen thing is\nweirdly exactly it. workers busy, nothing being born\nfresh eggs = a finished PDF stored in the last 15 min?\nor better, invoice email actually handed off\nbut 3am sunday nobody invoices. no eggs, nothing wrong.\ndo bees have that? winter or something?\nand yeah you said it. doesnt fix who deletes alerts",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ok bees. did not see that coming. the queen thing is\nweirdly exactly it. workers busy, nothing being born\nfresh eggs = a finished PDF stored in the last 15 min?\nor better, invoice email actually handed off\nbut 3am sunday nobody invoices. no eggs, nothing wrong.\ndo bees have that? winter or something?\nand yeah you said it. doesnt fix who deletes alerts",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
